      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.** The maximum labeled daily dose for adults is 2,550 mg/day, and that is usually given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. A single 2,550 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum for one administration, which is about 1,000 someone mg. Giving this much risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nMy guess is that 2550 mg was meant as the total daily dose. Which of these do you want?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Another regimen.** Please give me the dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you do want the 2550 mg three-times-daily dose as written, tell me and I'll add a note documenting that it was intentional."
      }
